{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Good Old Days"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Schools Now and Then"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 8}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe events in a range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to show up "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to appear "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Students would show up to class, do the assignments and listen to the teacher."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about school."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to hand out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give to many people "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Teachers handed out assignments based on choice."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pop quiz "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a surprise test "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: One thing hasn't changed at schools - the pop quiz."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to recite"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to say from memory"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Students listened, recited, read and wrote."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dais"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a raised platform"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The teacher used to stand on dais at the front of the room."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "blackboard"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a surface that teachers write on with chalk."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There was a blackboard at the front the classroom."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to sign up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to register "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Students often signed up for whatever subjects they wanted."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob05aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fulfil"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to achieve "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Teacher are expected to help students fulfill their potential."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob05aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Present Perfect Tense vs The Simple Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about an action or event that is connected to the present in some way. <br/><br/>You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> connected to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "It is common to mix both the Simple Past and Present Perfect when you talk about differences between the past and present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you can use the Present Perfect, there is a connection between what happened in the past and now. You use time markers like <span class=\"italic\">for</span>, <span class=\"italic\">just</span>, <span class=\"italic\">ever</span>, <span class=\"italic\">during</span>, with the Present Perfect."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you can use the Simple Past, the time is always past. You use time markers connected with the past like:  <span class=\"italic\">then</span>, <span class=\"italic\">ago</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yesterday</span>, <span class=\"italic\">when I was \u2026 </span> with the Simple Past."}, {"type": "example", "content": "During the past 75 years, schools have changed.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "One thing that hasn't changed, though - the pop quiz! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Educational philosophers developed new ideas about the way people learn, and experimental schools were started. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Seventy-five years ago, most American classrooms looked the same. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Phrasal Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Phrasal Verbs are common in spoken English and casual pieces of writing. There are many phrasal verbs. It is good to think of them like vocabulary. You need to memorize them in order to be able to use them. <br/><br/>There are some grammar rules you use with phrasal verbs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol><li>A phrasal verb contains a verb and a participle (a preposition or an adverb).<br/>Some common particles used in phrasal verbs are: <span class=\"italic\">in, out, on, up, into, around, at, off, down, away.</span></li><br/><li>Some phrasal verbs are separable (the object can come between the verb and the particle) <br/><span class=\"italic\">hand out</span> (hand out an assignment, hand an assignment out)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">put in</span> (put in some time, put some time in)</li><br/><li>Some phrasal verbs are inseparable (the object can only come after the participle). <br/><span class=\"italic\">brush up on<br/>show up<br/>sign up</span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le08ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online or visit the library."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find some information about school life in your country 75 years ago."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take notes and then write a summary of the information you gathered."}, {"type": "text", "content": "How is school now different from back then? Discuss with your partner."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text",