en used to help learners work at their own level and speed. One thing that hasn't changed, though - the pop quiz!", "id": 3, "image": "engenn7le08ob05re2img01.jpg"}], "coverimg": "engenn7le08ob05re2img01.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": ""}, {"time": "100", "text": "Seventy-five years ago, most American classrooms looked the same. The students used to sit in straight rows. There was a blackboard at the front of the room with a dais for the teacher. Students listened, recited, read, and wrote. They would show up for class, listen to the teacher and brush up on specific subjects.", "id": 1, "image": ""}, {"time": "21500", "text": "During the past 75 years, schools have changed. Educational philosophers developed new ideas about the way people learn, and experimental schools were started. In these special schools, students had a great deal of freedom. Students often signed up for whatever subjects they wanted. Instead of tests, students prepared projects, gave lectures, or conducted research.", "id": 2, "image": ""}, {"time": "48000", "text": "We can see the influence of these experimental schools in the modern classroom. Today, most children have more freedom of choice than their parents had. They are encouraged to study subjects that interest them. They write papers about subjects of their choice. Teachers are expected to help students fulfil their individual potential and hand out assignments based on choice. Computers are often used to help learners work at their own level and speed. One thing that hasn't changed, though - the pop quiz!", "id": 3, "image": ""}], "video_src": "engenn7le08ob05re2vid01"}}], "id": 2, "template_override": 1, "type": "video", "title": "", "_data": []}], "id": 0}]}